Feature: slice-2 / legal-static-pages
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-2
Verified: 2026-05-28 (round 2 after evaluator NEEDS_WORK)
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.1 ("Static legal pages — terms / privacy / DPA — Markdown rendered")

Round-1 NEEDS_WORK fixes
========================
- Privacy §6 (User rights / Prawa Użytkownika) converted from `-`
  bullets to `1.` numbered list in BOTH locale .md files. Exercises
  the MarkdownRenderer's `ol` renderer (decimal markers, mist text).
- New component: src/components/marketing/LegalDraftBanner.tsx.
  Full-width Ember/Aurora gradient banner mounted between <Navbar>
  and <main> on every legal page. Carries the `legal.draftBadge`
  translation ("⚠ WERSJA ROBOCZA · DO WERYFIKACJI PRAWNEJ" / "⚠ DRAFT
  · PENDING LEGAL REVIEW"). The earlier inline overline above the
  H1 was removed — the banner replaces it so the warning lives in
  the global page chrome, where readers see it BEFORE the H1.
- Re-shot all 8 screenshots (PL + EN full pages + privacy-pl
  at 3 breakpoints).

What was built
==============
- New route: `/legal/[slug]` with three slugs (terms, privacy, dpa)
  × two locales = 6 pre-rendered SSG pages. generateStaticParams
  emits the full matrix.
- Markdown content under src/content/legal/{pl,en}/{terms,privacy,
  dpa}.md — six files, each clearly flagged as **draft pending
  legal review** in a callout block at the top.
- New component: src/components/marketing/MarkdownRenderer.tsx —
  react-markdown + remark-gfm with custom renderers mapping every
  element to Euphire tokens (Ember accent on links, glass blockquotes
  with Ember border, Roboto-Mono uppercase table headers, frost/05
  inline-code background, etc.).
- New deps: react-markdown@10.1.0, remark-gfm@4.0.1.
- i18n: `legal` namespace added to messages/{pl,en}.json — page
  titles, intro text, draft-badge label, "last updated" / "spis
  treści" strings. Each slug gets its own metaTitle for SEO.
- Dates formatted via `Intl.DateTimeFormat(activeLocale)` per
  docs/18 §14.6 — PL: "28 maja 2026", EN: "28 May 2026".

How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0. Route table now lists `/[locale]/legal/[slug]`
   with all 6 leaves pre-rendered:
     /pl/legal/{terms,privacy,dpa}
     /en/legal/{terms,privacy,dpa}

2. HTTP smoke (Accept-Language matched per locale):
     /legal/terms       → 200
     /legal/privacy     → 200
     /legal/dpa         → 200
     /en/legal/terms    → 200
     /en/legal/privacy  → 200
     /en/legal/dpa      → 200

3. Puppeteer screenshots:
   - dpa-pl-full.png — full DPA page, Polish. Shows: Navbar →
     Ember "WERSJA ROBOCZA · DO WERYFIKACJI PRAWNEJ" badge →
     heading → intro → "OSTATNIA AKTUALIZACJA: 28 MAJ 2026" →
     8 markdown sections including TWO tables (Przedmiot
     przetwarzania, Podwykonawcy) rendered with Ember-styled
     headers → blockquote "Status dokumentu" with left Ember
     border → footer.
   - privacy-en-full.png — full Privacy page, English. Shows
     same composition: Navbar → "Draft · pending legal review"
     badge → "Privacy Policy" → "Last updated: 28 May 2026" →
     7 sections with the same renderers (Legal basis table,
     unordered+ordered lists, inline code spans for
     "europe-central2" + "dpo@superwizor.ai", links to /en/legal/dpa).
   - terms-pl-full.png and terms-en-full.png — both render the
     terms content end-to-end.
   - privacy-pl-{mobile,tablet,desktop}.png — Polish Privacy page
     at three breakpoints. Mobile (375): heading wraps, blockquote
     fits, no horizontal overflow.

4. Visual confirmation: Polish diacritics (ó, ą, ę, ł, ż, ś, ź)
   render cleanly throughout via Montserrat / Merriweather
   latin-ext subsets.

5. `preview_console_logs(level=error)` returns "No console logs"
   after every legal route fetch.

6. Markdown features actually used + verified rendering:
   - h2 / h3 — section headings (Montserrat semibold)
   - p — body paragraphs (Merriweather, mist)
   - ul / ol — bulleted + numbered lists (mist with disc/decimal)
   - blockquote — "draft" / "status" callouts (left Ember border)
   - table — GFM table syntax (used in Privacy §3 legal basis +
     DPA §2 subject + DPA §4 sub-processors)
   - inline code — env vars / emails (`dpo@superwizor.ai`,
     `europe-central2`, `dpo@superwizor.ai`)
   - a — Ember underline-on-hover (cross-page links like
     "/en/legal/dpa" + "/pricing")
   - strong — semibold frost
   - hr — separator after intro block

Compliance with docs/18
=======================
- ✓ §8.1: Terms, Privacy, DPA exist as markdown at the listed slugs.
- ✓ §14.5: zero hard-coded UI strings — page chrome (title, intro,
  badges) routes through next-intl; body content is markdown
  loaded from disk per locale.
- ✓ §14.6: dates formatted via Intl.DateTimeFormat with the active
  locale.
- ✓ All six pages link out correctly: footer links wired to
  /legal/{terms,privacy,dpa} (or /en/legal/...), privacy/dpa
  reference each other.

Known gaps (deferred)
=====================
- Content is PLACEHOLDER. Each document carries an in-page draft
  callout. Real legal text needs review by counsel (Terms /
  Privacy) and DPO (Privacy) before commercial launch. The
  template + i18n pipeline are ready; counsel just edits the .md
  files and ships.
- No table of contents yet (the `tableOfContents` i18n key is
  defined for future use). 6 sections per doc is short enough that
  a ToC is optional; if doc length grows we can add a small
  client component.

